PLACEHOLDER-DO-NOT-USE
# This file documents where the api_ro role's password secret lives. Do not use
# this value and do not copy this file to api_db_password.txt. Generate a real
# one, then enable the role's login (scripts/set-api-ro-password.sh):
#   openssl rand -base64 32 > secrets/api_db_password.txt
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD/secrets:/s" postgres:18.4-trixie \
#     sh -c 'chown 65532:65532 /s/api_db_password.txt && chmod 600 /s/api_db_password.txt'
#   ./scripts/set-api-ro-password.sh
# Rotation: repeat the same three steps, then re-run set-api-ro-password.sh —
# it always ALTERs the role to the file's current contents.
